From 959258a4adbe442b3362c2ada559d191fad933a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:43:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] es_out: a seek ends the next-frame mode

Paused, after next frames (frame stepping on), a precise seek (a frame
back) ran in the next-frame mode, which only the end of the pause ends:
it showed the picture after its target, another one after that for a
moment, and the next seek went two back (Amlogic, Dolby Vision profile
8: video_composer's frame index 115 -> 116 instead of 114, then 113).
The seek now ends it; the next frame starts it again.

Message-Id: <20261111-dvfel-es-out-seek-ends-next-frame@djnice>
---
 src/input/es_out.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
index 981803c..b01aa0c 100644
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -2978,6 +2978,11 @@ static int EsOutControlLocked( es_out_t *out, int i_query, va_list args )
 
         assert( i_date == -1 );
         EsOutChangePosition( out );
+        /* A seek ends the next-frame mode (the next frame starts it again):
+         * kept, the precise seek that follows frame steps (paused, a frame
+         * back) showed a picture after its target, and another one after
+         * that for a moment (Amlogic, measured), the next seek two back */
+        p_sys->p_next_frame_es = NULL;
 
         return VLC_SUCCESS;
     }
-- 
